Package: ldfreq
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Lexical Diversity and Frequency Profiles
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Ryuya",
        family = "Komuro",
        email = "komuro.4121@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Computes twelve versioned lexical-diversity metrics from ordered token
    vectors and from raw English text. Results record the selected formula,
    parameters, token and type counts, and preprocessing choices such as Unicode
    normalization, case handling, lemmatization, and content-word selection.
    Separate functions compare Maas and sequential-MTLD definitions, expose
    local MATTR windows and positional exposure, compute exact term-set or
    annotated content-word overlap, and measure token- and type-weighted
    coverage of multiple documents by one explicit reference set. Caller-
    supplied lexical norm tables can be summarized with exact matching,
    measure-level provenance, and separate resource and annotation coverage.
    Lexical level profiles use a caller-supplied New
    JACET 8000 list and report exact and cumulative token- and type-weighted
    coverage without redistributing the list. A bundled, versioned TUBELEX
    aggregate provides frequency, video
    prevalence, and channel prevalence profiles with explicit match coverage.
    Convenience adapters accept tidy token tables and 'quanteda' token objects;
    deterministic wide reshaping and base-R plots support analysis workflows.
